@startuml
!include ../../_style.iuml
' Derived from: crates/openmeet-core/src/types.rs (RequestSlot, RequestKind),
' crates/openmeet-engine/src/requests.rs (Slots { current, entries }, begin, is_current, emit_if_current, set_state, cancel, cancel_all),
' crates/openmeet-engine/src/assist.rs (start_primary, interviewer follow-ups, background begin calls), crates/openmeet-engine/src/screen.rs
title Request slots - RequestManager.current pointer per exclusive RequestSlot (Primary, Followups)

hide empty description
skinparam StateFontSize 12
left to right direction

state "No current request\n(slot not in Slots.current)" as Empty

state "Occupied: Slots.current[slot] = id" as Occupied {
  state "Request running\n(AnswerState not terminal)" as Running : is_current(ticket) = true\nemit_if_current: AnswerDelta, FollowupsReady,\nAnswerComplete delivered
  state "Request finished\n(Complete / Failed / Cancelled)" as Finished : pointer kept, so late events of\nolder requests stay suppressed
  Running --> Finished : set_state(terminal)\n/ emit AnswerStateChanged
  Running --> Finished : cancel(request_id)\n(cancel_request, dismiss_suggestion)\nor cancel_all(..)
}

[*] --> Empty
Empty --> Running : begin(slot, kind)\n/ emit AnswerStarted
Occupied --> Running : begin(slot, kind) / previous ticket\ncancelled -> Cancelled, then\nemit AnswerStarted (under slot lock)

note bottom of Occupied
  Slot use (begin call sites):
  Primary   - CandidateAnswer, AskAi, Refinement, Clarification, CatchUp (start_primary)
  Followups - InterviewerFollowups
  Background (never exclusive, not tracked in Slots.current; cancelled only by
  cancel_all(true) / cancel(id)): QuestionClassification, Compression,
  TopicAnalysis, Summary, ScreenAnalysis.
  The finished entry of a request that is no longer current is dropped
  from Slots.entries; the current one is kept until the next begin.
end note
@enduml
